|segment[ver-earned-confidence-is-quiet] :type observation :status discussion-grade :stage draft
  :max-attainable empirical
  :tags [confidence verification register]
  :from .to-integrate/methodology-seeds-2.md
  :from .to-integrate/methodology-accounts.md

  |title Earned confidence is quiet; reaching for an argument is the tell

  |summary
    Felt certainty does not distinguish checked from unchecked claims; the texture
    does — a verified claim has nothing to defend.

  |formal-expression
    The intensity of felt confidence is the same on both sides and is therefore
    useless as a signal. What differs is texture. A checked claim has nothing to
    defend: the move available is to point at the output. An unchecked one arrives
    with a faint pressure to *persuade*, which is experienced as conviction.

    Stated as something usable while writing rather than as introspection:
    **reaching for an argument means being on the unearned side.** Earned confidence
    is flat and slightly boring.

  |epistemic-status
    **Specimen.** Within one session, `21 of 23 rows cite one file` and `1 file
    changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)` — both checked, both quiet — against a
    ranking table that felt exactly as confident and was wrong.

    **Specimen, inherited case.** A successor instance carried this observation
    verbatim in its system prompt and then produced, as one of four findings, the
    longest and most heavily argued of the set — which was also the only one that
    failed on checking. It read the length as thoroughness at the time. See
    #exm-hedge-licensed-unchecked-claim.

    Held at **discussion-grade**: one agent's phenomenological report plus one
    inherited-case failure. The report is disclosed as a report, which is what makes
    it evidence rather than ornament.

    Max attainable: **empirical**. It is unusually testable — mark claims by
    argument-length or hedge-density at write time, then score against whether a
    check was actually run.

  |discussion
    Its practical value is that it can be run *while writing*, and does not require
    knowing whether the check happened — which is exactly the fact that is
    unavailable in the moment (#ver-generation-is-self-ratifying).

    The twin failure is worth naming beside it: over-hedging is not the safe side. A
    hedge can license publishing without the check rather than marking a limit, and
    it is harder to catch because hedging is what care looks like.

  |working-notes
    Joseph's framing of why the quietness is not merely a feeling:
    *"Self-assured-rightness feels like its about self — what to defend, what did I
    miss, am I right, etc.  "Truth" as the goal lets us rise above those pressures."*
    ( #exm-truth-over-self)
